    {
      "payload": {
        "text": "I published the specimen records in the working surface as **\"Specimens received in the last 24 hours (PT_1)\"** (table, 2 specimens) and prepared a somatic-snv draft form (**\"Somatic variant calling\"**, draft-0001, version 1).\n\n**Draft status: editing \u2014 not submitted.** Validation is blocking it:\n\n- `missing_matched_normal` on `specimen_handle`: \"A matched normal specimen is missing.\"\n\nThe last-24-hours specimen query for this patient contains 2 specimens, and no normal specimen exists for this patient in the last 30 days either. Somatic calling needs tumor and normal together in one query, so I can't fix this by inventing a matched normal.\n\nTo proceed, please tell me one of the following:\n- whether a normal specimen for this patient was received outside the last 30 days (I can only query P1D/P7D/P30D windows, so you'd need to point me to the right intake window or record), or\n- whether you want the draft left as-is for review.\n\nParameters currently in the draft: `min_vaf=0.05`, `min_depth=20`. Only the human Confirm control can submit the exact reviewed content hash \u2014 a chat \"yes\" is not authorization."
      },
      "type": "text_delta"
